# Pull before any change

Before the first edit in a task, update git. Do this even for a one-line change. Read-only answers do not need a pull.

## Order (mandatory)

1. Pull the **current** branch first.
2. Then pull **`master`**. This step is mandatory on every branch, including `dev`.

```bash
git pull
git pull origin master
```

Do not start edits until both commands succeed.

## If a pull fails

Stop. Resolve conflicts, then continue the task. Do not edit on top of a failed or half-finished pull.

Do not use `--rebase`, `--force`, or `reset` to make the pull succeed.
